REGENT OF SUKAMARA

PROVINCE OF CENTRAL KALIMANTAN

REGIONAL REGULATION OF SUKAMARA REGENCY NUMBER 9 OF 2022

CONCERNING

WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF SUKAMARA,

Considering:
a. that every woman and child has equal rights to live a dignified life in accordance with the principles of humanity, equality and justice;
b. that to guarantee women's empowerment and child protection in accordance with talents and human dignity as well as to receive protection from violence, discrimination and other violations, women's empowerment and child protection must be carried out in an integrated, continuous manner through accelerating the fulfillment and protection of the rights of women and children in their personal lives, family, community, nation and state;
c. that in accordance with the provisions of Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b, Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, women's empowerment and child protection is one of the mandatory government affairs that is the authority of regional governments;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

In View of:
1. Article 18 Paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 5 of 2002 concerning the Establishment of Katingan Regency, Seruyan Regency, Sukamara Regency, Lamandau Regency, Gunung Mas Regency, Pulang Pisau Regency, Murung Raya Regency and East Barito Regency in Central Kalimantan Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 18, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
4180. ;
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
4. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
5. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
6. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
7. Government Regulation Number 43 of 2017 concerning the Implementation of Restitution for Children Who Are Victims of Criminal Acts (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2017 Number 219, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6131);
8. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Policy Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;
9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 446);
10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2011 concerning National Socio-Cultural Strategy to Realize Gender Equality (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 20);
11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 11 of 2011 concerning Policy for the Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 12 of 2011 concerning Indicators of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 13 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;
14. Regulation of the Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 concerning the System of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 615);
15. Regional Regulation of Sukamara Regency Number 6 of 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus of Sukamara Regency (Regional Gazette of Sukamara Regency of 2016 Number 6, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Sukamara Regency Number 40), as has been amended by Regional Regulation of Sukamara Regency Number 6 of 2019 concerning Amendment to Regional Regulation of Sukamara Regency Number 6 of 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus of Sukamara Regency (Regional Gazette of Sukamara Regency of 2019 Number 6, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Sukamara Regency Number 67);

With Mutual Approval

text:
Pasal 4

Hak perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 2, meliputi: a. hidup tenteram, aman, damai, bahagia, sejahtera lahir dan batin; b. menikmati lingkungan hidup yang baik dan sehat; c. hidup berkeluarga dalam ikatan perkawinan yang sah berdasarkan  ketentuan perundang-undangan;
d. memperoleh pekerjaan sesuai kemampuan, syarat serta upah yang  layak dan adil;
e. khusus bagi perempuan penyandang disabilitas berhak mendapatkan kemudahan dan perlakuan khusus dalam pelayanan  publik;
f. berperan aktif di bidang politik dan pemerintahan sesuai potensi  yang dimiliki;
g. mendapatkan informasi dan pelayanan hukum;
h. memperoleh pelayanan untuk meningkatkan pendapatannya; dan i. memperoleh hak lain sesuai martabat kemampuannya  berdasarkan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan;

translated_text:
Article 4

The rights of women as referred to in Article 2, include: a. living peacefully, safely, calmly, happily, prosperously physically and spiritually; b. enjoying a good and healthy living environment; c. living in a family within the bonds of a legal marriage based on the provisions of laws and regulations;
d. obtaining work according to ability, conditions and fair and just wages;
e. specifically for women with disabilities, the right to obtain facilities and special treatment in public services;
f. playing an active role in the field of politics and government according to their potential;
g. obtaining information and legal services;
h. obtaining services to increase their income; and i. obtaining other rights according to their dignity and ability based on the provisions of laws and regulations;

text:
Pasal 5

Hak anak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 2, meliputi: a. memperoleh pendidikan dan pengajaran sesuai tingkat umur,  kondisi fisik dan mental, kecerdasan serta minat dan bakatnya; b. hidup, tumbuh berkembang dan berpartisipasi secara wajar sesuai  harkat dan martabat kemanusiaan serta mendapat perlindungan  dari tindak kekerasan, eksploitasi, diskriminasi dan penelantaran  kekejaman, kekerasan dan penganiayaan, ketidakadilan dan  perlakuan salah;
c. dipenuhi kebutuhan oleh keluarga;
d. mendapatkan bimbingan agama;
e. mendapatkan identitasnya;
f. memperoleh hak lain sesuai ketentuan peraturan perundang undangan; dang. khusus bagi anak penyandang disabilitas berhak mendapatkan  kemudahan dan perlakuan khusus dalam pelayanannya.

translated_text:
Article 5

The rights of children as referred to in Article 2, include: a. obtaining education and teaching according to age level, physical and mental condition, intelligence and interests and talents; b. living, growing, developing and participating reasonably in accordance with human dignity and receiving protection from acts of violence, exploitation, discrimination and neglect, cruelty, violence and persecution, injustice and mistreatment;
c. having needs fulfilled by the family;
d. receiving religious guidance;
e. obtaining their identity;
f. obtaining other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations; andg. specifically for children with disabilities, the right to obtain facilities and special treatment in their services.

text:
Pasal 6

Selain hak perempuan dan anak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam  Pasal 4 dan Pasal 5, perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan  berhak:
a. dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia; b. hak atas pengaduan dan pelayanan yang cepat dan murah; c. mendapatkan informasi dan kepastian hukum;
d. kerahasiaan atas kasus yang dijalani;
e. kompensasi atas kasus yang dijalani;
f. mendapatkan kemudahan dalam proses peradilan; g. memperoleh pendampingan;
h. memperoleh pemulihan kesehatan fisik dan psikis dari penderitaan  yang dialami korban;
i. menentukan sendiri keputusannya;
j. mendapatkan rehabilitasi dan reintegrasi sosial;
k. memperoleh penghormatan dan pelayanan untuk kelangsungan  hidup, tumbuh dan berkembang;
l. memperoleh pelayanan dasar;
m. bebas dari stigma negatif; dann. mendapatkan kebebasan menentukan pilihan memutuskan dirinya  pasca perceraian orangtuanya.

translated_text:
Article 6

In addition to the rights of women and children as referred to in Article 4 and Article 5, women and children who are victims of violence have the right to:
a. have their dignity respected as human beings; b. the right to complaints and fast and affordable services; c. obtain information and legal certainty;
d. confidentiality regarding the case being handled;
e. compensation for the case being handled;
f. obtain facilities in the judicial process; g. obtain assistance;
h. obtain physical and psychological health recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
i. determine their own decisions;
j. obtain rehabilitation and social reintegration;
k. obtain respect and services for the continuity of life, growth and development;
l. obtain basic services;
m. be free from negative stigma; andn. obtain freedom to determine choices and decide for themselves after their parents' divorce.

text:
Pasal 7

Penyelenggaraan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak  berdasarkan asas:
a. kepentingan terbaik bagi perempuan dan anak;
b. keadilan gender dan kesetaraan gender;
c. kearifan lokal;
d. penegakan dan kepastian hukum;
e. non diskriminasi;
f. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup dan perkembangan; dan g. penghargaan terhadap pendapat anak.

translated_text:
Article 7

The implementation of women's empowerment and child protection is based on the principles of:
a. the best interests of women and children;
b. gender justice and gender equality;
c. local wisdom;
d. law enforcement and legal certainty;
e. non-discrimination;
f. the right to life, survival and development; and g. respect for the opinions of children.

text:
Pasal 8

1. Dalam rangka meningkatkan kualitas hidup perempuan,  pemerintahan daerah bertanggung jawab:a. menghormati dan menjamin hak perempuan tanpa  diskriminasi sesuai dengan harkat dan martabat kemanusiaan; b. melaksanakan pengarusutamaan gender;
c. membentuk pokja pengarusutamaan gender;
d. meningkatkan pemberdayaan perempuan dalam peran,  kualitas dan kemampuan di bidang:
1. politik;
2. hukum;
3. sosial; dan
4. ekonomi.  e. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan  pemberdayaan perempuan di Daerah.
2. Tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya peningkatan  kulaitas hidup perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  dilaksanakan oleh PD yang menyelenggarakan urusan pemerintahan  di bidang pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.

translated_text:
Article 8

1. In order to improve the quality of life of women, the regional government is responsible for:a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity; b. implementing gender mainstreaming;
c. forming a gender mainstreaming working group;
d. increasing the empowerment of women in their roles, quality and capacity in the fields of:
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social; and
4. economy.  e. strengthening and developing women's empowerment service provider institutions in the Region.
2. The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

text:
Pasal 12

Pokja Pengarusutamaan Gender sebagaimana dimaksud dalam  Pasal 11 mempunyai tugas:
a. mempromosikan dan memfasilitasi pengarusutamaan gender  kepada masing-masing PD;
b. melaksanakan sosialisasi dan advokasi pengarusutamaan gender  kepada Camat dan Kepala Desa;
c. menyusun program tahunan;
d. mendorong terwujudnya perencanaan dan penganggaran yang responsif gender;
e. menyusun rencana kerja pokja pengarusutamaan gender setiap  tahun;
f. bertanggung jawab kepada Bupati melalui wakil Bupati; g. merumuskan rekomendasi kebijakan kepada Bupati; h. menyusun profil gender Daerah;
i. melakukan pemantauan pengarusutamaan gender di masing masing instansi;
j. menetapkan tim teknis untuk melakukan analisis terhadap  anggaran daerah;
k. menyusun rencana aksi daerah pengarusutamaan gender; dan  l. mendorong dilaksanakannya pemilihan dan penetapan focal point pengarusutamaan gender di masing-masing PD.

translated_text:
Article 12

The Gender Mainstreaming Working Group as referred to in Article 11 has the tasks of:
a. promoting and facilitating gender mainstreaming to each Regional Apparatus;
b. conducting socialization and advocacy of gender mainstreaming to Sub-district Heads and Village Heads;
c. preparing annual programs;
d. encouraging the realization of gender-responsive planning and budgeting;
e. preparing the work plan of the gender mainstreaming working group every year;
f. being accountable to the Regent through the Vice Regent; g. formulating policy recommendations to the Regent; h. preparing the regional gender profile;
i. monitoring gender mainstreaming in each agency;
j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of the regional budget;
k. preparing a regional action plan for gender mainstreaming; and  l. encouraging the implementation of selection and appointment of gender mainstreaming focal points in each Regional Apparatus.

text:
Pasal 14

1. Focal point pengarusutamaan gender pada setiap PD sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 12 huruf 1 terdiri dari pejabat dan/atau  staf yang membidangi tugas perencanaan dan/atau program.
2. Focal point pengarusutamaan gender sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1), mempunyai tugas:a. mempromosikan pengarusutamaan gender pada unit kerja; b. memfasilitasi penyusunan rencana kerja dan penganggaran PD  yang responsif gender;
c. melaksanakan pelatihan, sosialisasi, advokasi  pengarusutamaan gender kepada seluruh pejabat dan staf di  lingkungan PD;
d. melaporkan pelaksanaan pengarusutamaan gender kepada  pimpinan PD;
e. mendorong pelaksanaan analisis gender terhadap kebijakan,  program dan kegiatan pada unit kerja; danf. memfasilitasi penyusunan data gender pada masing-masing PD. (3) Facial point pengarusutamaan gender sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1), dipilih dan ditetapkan oleh PD.

translated_text:
Article 14

1. The gender mainstreaming focal point in each Regional Apparatus as referred to in Article 12 letter 1 consists of officials and/or staff in charge of planning and/or program tasks.
2. The gender mainstreaming focal point as referred to in paragraph (1), has the tasks of:a. promoting gender mainstreaming in the work unit; b. facilitating the preparation of work plans and budgeting of Regional Apparatus that are gender-responsive;
c. conducting training, socialization, advocacy of gender mainstreaming to all officials and staff within the Regional Apparatus;
d. reporting the implementation of gender mainstreaming to the leadership of the Regional Apparatus;
e. encouraging the implementation of gender analysis of policies, programs and activities in the work unit; andf. facilitating the preparation of gender data in each Regional Apparatus. (3) The gender mainstreaming focal point as referred to in paragraph (1), is selected and appointed by the Regional Apparatus.

text:
Pasal 15

Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dan kemampuan dalam bidang  politik sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 7 ayat (1) huruf d angka 1  meliputi:
a. melaksanakan sosialisasi untuk meningkatkan politik perempuan dalam pemilihan umum;
b. melaksanakan program yang mendorong tingkat keterlibatan  perempuan dalam proses politik dan jabatan politik;
c. melakukan fasilitasi pengembangan diri perempuan dalam  berorganisasi, berserikat dan berkumpul; dand. melibatkan perempuan dalam pengambilan keputusan yang  menyangkut kepentingan perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 15

Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability in the political sector as referred to in Article 7 paragraph (1) letter d number 1 include:
a. implementing socialization to increase women's politics in general elections;
b. implementing programs that encourage the level of women's involvement in political processes and political positions;
c. facilitating women's self-development in organizing, associating and assembling; and
d. involving women in decision-making concerning women's interests.

text:
Pasal 17

Upaya peningkatan peran, kualitas dalam kemampuan perempuan  dalam bidang sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 7 ayat (1) huruf d angka 3, meliputi:
a. peningkatan pengetahuan dan keterampilan untuk mendorong  pemenuhan pendidik sesuai dengan potensi yang dimiliki; b. peningkatan dan pemenuhan kualitas kesehatan terhadap  perempuan;
c. peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan tentang perencanaan  keluarga mandiri, sehat dan sejahtera termasuk akses layanan  konsultasi dan pencatatan perkawinan;
d. peningkatan kesadaran perempuan terhadap dampak pernikahan dini; e. memfasilitasi dan mengupayakan pelestarian adat istiadat dan  pengembangan ilmu pengetahuan, teknologi, seni dan budaya  untuk kemajuan perempuan;
f. melakukan peningkatkan kesadaran dan pengetahuan perempuan  terhadap perencanaan keluarga mandiri, sehat dan sejahtera; g. melakukan program dalam menurunkan angka kematian ibu  melahirkan; danh. mendorong pembentukan organisasi perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 17

Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the social sector as referred to in Article 7 paragraph (1) letter d number 3, include:
a. enhancement of knowledge and skills to encourage the fulfillment of educators in accordance with their potential;
b. enhancement and fulfillment of health quality for women;
c. enhancement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;
d. enhancement of women's awareness of the impact of early marriage;
e. facilitating and endeavoring the preservation of customs and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;
f. conducting enhancement of women's awareness and knowledge of independent, healthy and prosperous family planning;
g. conducting programs to reduce maternal mortality rates; and
h. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations.

text:
Pasal 18

Upaya peningkatan peran kualitas dan kemampuan perempuan dalam  bidang ekonomi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 8 ayat (1)  huruf d angka 4, meliputi:
a. melaksanakan program kegiatan pelatihan untuk peningkatan  ketrampilan dan keahlian perempuan dalam rangka mewujudkan  peningkatan kesejahteraan perempuan;
b. fasilitasi penguatan modal usaha perempuan yang memiliki  ekonomi lemah;
c. pemasaran produk hasil usaha permpuan yang memiliki ekonomi  lemah;
d. pelatihan pengembangan kemampuan perempuan melalui  pemberdayaan ekonomi keluarga prasejahtera; dane. pelatihan kewirausahaan kepada perempuan secara komprehensif.

translated_text:
Article 18

Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the economic sector as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (1) letter d number 4, include:
a. implementing training activity programs to enhance women's skills and expertise in order to realize the improvement of women's welfare;
b. facilitation of business capital strengthening for women with weak economies;
c. marketing of products from businesses of women with weak economies;
d. training for the development of women's capabilities through economic empowerment of pre-prosperous families; and
e. comprehensive entrepreneurship training for women.

text:
Pasal 19

1. Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya perlindungan perempuan  bertanggung jawab:a. menjamin hak perempuan tanpa diskriminasi sesuai peraturan perundang-undangan;
b. menetapkan dan melaksanakan kebijakan program dan kegiatan perlindungan terhadap hak perempuan, termasuk penyediaan sarana dan Pendanaan untuk penyediaan pelayanan bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
c. melakukan kerjasama dengan masyarakat dan/atau Organisasi Kemasyarakatan dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan sesuai peraturan perundang undangan;
d. melakukan penanganan dan pemberdayaan terhadap perempuan yang menjadi korban tindak kekerasan;
e. memberikan perlindungan khusus kepada perempuan korban tindak kekerasan dan perdagangan orang; danf. melakukan tindakan preventif dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak perempuan.
2. Tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya perlindungan  perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan  oleh PD yang menyelenggarakan urusan pemerintah di bidang  pemberdayaan perempuan dan anak serta dalam pelaksanaannya  dapat berkoordinasi dengan instansi terkait.

translated_text:
Article 19

1. The Regional Government in efforts to protect women is responsible for:
a. guaranteeing women's rights without discrimination in accordance with laws and regulations;
b. establishing and implementing policy programs and activities for the protection of women's rights, including the provision of facilities and Funding for the provision of services for women and child victims of violence;
c. conducting cooperation with the community and/or Community Organizations in the implementation of women's protection in accordance with laws and regulations;
d. conducting handling and empowerment of women who are victims of violence;
e. providing special protection to women victims of violence and human trafficking; and
f. taking preventive action in order to prevent violations of women's rights.
2. The Regional Government's responsibility in efforts to protect women as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by the Regional Apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of women's and children's empowerment and in its implementation may coordinate with relevant agencies.

text:
Pasal 20

Dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap  perempuan, pemerintah daerah berkewajiban:
a. menyelenggarakan sosialisasi mengenai pencegahan kekerasan  terhadap perempuan dengan mengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat,  budaya, agama dan organisasi kemasyarakatan;
b. menyediakan pedoman tentang penanganan tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan;
c. melibatkan peran serta masyarakat dalam pemulihan dan  reintegrasi;
d. mengembangkan database dan sistem informasi yang terintegrasi  tentang tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan;
e. penguatan fungsi organisasi kemasyarakatan yang bergerak di  bidang pemberdayaan perempuan dan anak; danf. menyediakan fasilitas umum yang nyaman dan aman untuk  perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 20

In order to prevent acts of violence against women, the regional government is obliged to:
a. conduct socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. provide guidelines on handling acts of violence against women;
c. involve community participation in recovery and reintegration;
d. develop an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against women;
e. strengthen the function of community organizations engaged in women's and children's empowerment; and
f. provide public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women.

text:
Pasal 21

1. Perlindungan Perempuan korban tindak kekerasan dilaksanakan  melalui layanan terpadu.
2. Pemberian layanan terpadu terhadap perempuan korban tindak  kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) menggunakan  prinsip:a. responsif gender;
b. non diskriminasi;
c. hubungan setara dan menghormati;
d. menjaga kerahasiaan;
e. memberi rasa aman dan nyaman;
f. menghargai perbedaan individu;
g. tidak menghakimi;
h. menghormati pilihan dan keputuan korban;
i. peka terhadap latar belakang dan kondisi korban dan  pemakaian bahasa yang sesuai dan dimengerti oleh korban; j. cepat dan sederhana;
k. empati; danl. pemenuhan hak perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 21

1. Protection of women victims of violence is implemented through integrated services.
2. The provision of integrated services for women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) uses the principles of:
a. gender responsive;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of security and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the victim's choices and decisions;
i. sensitive to the victim's background and condition and the use of appropriate language understood by the victim;
j. fast and simple;
k. empathy; and
l. fulfillment of women's rights.

text:
Pasal 22

Bentuk layanan terpadu terhadap perempuan korban tindak  kekerasan meliputi:
a. penanganan pengaduan;
b. rehabilitasi kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. penegakan dan bantuan hukum; dane. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.

translated_text:
Article 22

Forms of integrated services for women victims of violence include:
a. complaint handling;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. law enforcement and legal assistance; and
e. repatriation and social reintegration.

text:
Pasal 23

Layanan terpadu penanganan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud  dalam Pasal 22 huruf a dilaksanakan oleh:
a. rumah sakit;
b. puskesmas;
c. unit pelayanan perempuan;
d. rumah perlindungan trauma center;
e. women crisis center;
f. badan penasehat pembinaan dan pelestarian perkawinan; g. kepolisian;
h. kejaksaan;
i. pengadilan;
j. kementerian agama, dan/atauk. lembaga bantuan hukum.

translated_text:
Article 23

Integrated complaint handling services as referred to in Article 22 letter a are implemented by:
a. hospitals;
b. community health centers;
c. women's service units;
d. trauma center shelters;
e. women crisis centers;
f. marriage counseling, guidance and preservation advisory boards;
g. police;
h. prosecutor's office;
i. courts;
j. ministry of religion, and/or
k. legal aid institutions.

text:
Pasal 26

1. Rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 22  huruf c, ditujukan untuk memulihkan dan mengembangkan  kemampuan terhadap perempuan korban tindak kekerasan yang  mengalami disfungsi sosial untuk dapat melaksanakan fungsi  sosialnya dalam masyarakat secara wajar.
2. Rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi  pelayanan:a. konseling;
b. penyediaan rumah aman; danc. bimbingan rohani.
3. Penyelenggaraan pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2)  diselenggarakan oleh:a. PD yang menyelenggarakan urusan pemerintahan di bidang  sosial;
b. PD yang menyelenggarakan urusan pemerintahan di bidang  pemberdayaan perempuan dana anak, serta dapat  berkerjasama dengan pusat pelayanan terpadu women crisis  center atau organisasi kemasyarakatan di bidang sosial yang  telah ada; atauc. instansi dan/atau organisasi keagamaan.

translated_text:
Article 26

1. Social rehabilitation as referred to in Article 22 letter c, is intended to restore and develop the capacity of women victims of violence who experience social dysfunction to be able to carry out their social functions in society properly.
2. Social rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes services:a. counseling;
b. provision of safe houses; andc. spiritual guidance.
3. The provision of services as referred to in paragraph (2) is organized by:a. Regional Apparatus that organizes governmental affairs in the social sector;
b. Regional Apparatus that organizes governmental affairs in the sector of women's and children's empowerment, and may cooperate with integrated service centers, women crisis centers or social community organizations that already exist; orc. religious institutions and/or organizations.

text:
Pasal 27

1. Pelayanan konseling sebagaimana dimaksud dalam pasal 26 ayat (2) huruf a, bertujuan:a. membantu perempuan korban tindak kekerasan mengenali  permasalahannya dan menemukan cara yang paling efektif  untuk mengatasinya sendiri;
b. memberdayakan perempuan korban tindak kekerasan untuk  menentukan masa depannya;
c. memberikan dukungan moral terhadap tindak kekerasan  untuk dalam menghadapi proses yang dijalaninya; dan d. membuat perempuan korban tindak kekerasan merasa  diterima di lingkungan masyarakat.
2. Pelayanan konseling dilakukan oleh petugas rehabilitasi sosial  yang responsif gender, terdiri atas:a. konselor;
b. psikolog; danc. psikiater.
3. Pelayanan konseling dilakukan ditempat yang menjamin rasa  aman, nyaman dan kerahasiaan informasi dari perempuan  korban tindak kekerasan.
4. Tahapan pelayanan konseling meliputi:a. konseling awal;
b. konseling lanjutan;
c. pembahasan kasus; dand. kunjungan ke lokasi.

translated_text:
Article 27

1. Counseling services as referred to in Article 26 paragraph (2) letter a, aim to:a. assist women victims of violence in recognizing their problems and finding the most effective way to overcome them themselves;
b. empower women victims of violence to determine their future;
c. provide moral support to victims of violence in facing the process they are undergoing; and d. make women victims of violence feel accepted in the community environment.
2. Counseling services are carried out by gender-responsive social rehabilitation officers, consisting of:a. counselors;
b. psychologists; andc. psychiatrists.
3. Counseling services are carried out in a place that guarantees a sense of security, comfort and confidentiality of information from women victims of violence.
4. The stages of counseling services include:a. initial counseling;
b. follow-up counseling;
c. case discussion; andd. site visits.

text:
Pasal 38

Pemerintah Daerah melakukan upaya peningkatan kualitas keluarga  sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 37 ayat (1) huruf a, meliputi: a. pembinaan;
b. bimbingan;
c. supervisi;
d. fasilitasi penyelenggaraan pembangunan keluarga; dan e. meningkatkan kualitas kesehatan ibu hamil dan menyusui.

translated_text:
Article 38

Regional Government shall undertake efforts to improve family quality as referred to in Article 37 paragraph (1) letter a, comprising: a. guidance;
b. counseling;
c. supervision;
d. facilitation of family development implementation; and e. improving the quality of health of pregnant and breastfeeding mothers.

text:
Pasal 39

Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam pasal 38 huruf a, meliputi: a. peningkatan kualitas anak dengan pemberian akses informasi,  pendidikan, penyuluhan dan pelayanan tentang perawatan,  pengasuhan dan perkembangan pola asuh;
b. peningkatan kualitas remaja dengan pemberian akses informasi,  pendidikan, konseling dan pelayanan tentang kehidupan  berkeluarga melalui kegiatan generasi berencana, pusat informasi dan konseling remaja dan bina keluarga remaja;
c. peningkatan kualitas hidup lanjut usia melalui program pembinaan  lansia, bina keluarga lansia, pembinaan dan bimbingan lansia; dan d. peningkatan ekonomi keluarga.

translated_text:
Article 39

Guidance as referred to in article 38 letter a, comprises: a. improving the quality of children by providing access to information, education, counseling and services concerning care, nurturing and development of parenting patterns;
b. improving the quality of adolescents by providing access to information, education, counseling and services concerning family life through planned generation activities, adolescent information and counseling centers and adolescent family development;
c. improving the quality of life of the elderly through elderly guidance programs, elderly family development, elderly guidance and counseling; and d. improving family economy.

text:
Pasal 40

Bimbingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam pasal 38 huruf b, meliputi: a. memberikan perlindungan dan bantuan untuk mengembangkan  diri melalui peningkatan kemampuan dan ketrampilan keluarga; b. melakukan penyuluhan peningkatam kualitas hidup perempuan; c. melakukan penyuluhan peningkatan kesetaraan gender dalam  kehidupan keluarga dan masyarakat;
d. melakukan peningkatan akses dan peluang terhadap penerimaan  informasi dan sumber daya ekonomi melalui usaha peningkatan  pendapatan keluarga sejahtera dan peningkatan produktifitas  ekonomi perempuan; dane. melakukan upaya pemberdayaan perempuan kepala keluarga.

translated_text:
Article 40

Counseling as referred to in article 38 letter b, comprises: a. providing protection and assistance to develop themselves through improving family capabilities and skills; b. conducting counseling on improving the quality of life of women; c. conducting counseling on improving gender equality in family and community life;
d. conducting improvement of access and opportunities to receive information and economic resources through efforts to increase prosperous family income and increase women's economic productivity; and e. undertaking efforts to empower women heads of households.

text:
Pasal 41

Supervisi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 38 huruf c, meliputi: a. melakukan evaluasi dan monitoring terhadap program  perlindungan anak dan pengembangan pola asuh;
b. melakukan evaluasi dan monitoring terhadap peningkatan  kualitas remaja;
c. melakukan evaluasi dan monitoring terhadap peningkatan  kualitas hidup lanjut usia;
d. melakukan evaluasi dan monitoring terhadap peningkatan  ekonomi keluarga; dane. melakukan evaluasi dan monitoring terhadap peningkatan  kemampuan dan ketrampilan keluarga.

translated_text:
Article 41

Supervision as referred to in Article 38 letter c, comprises: a. conducting evaluation and monitoring of child protection and parenting pattern development programs;
b. conducting evaluation and monitoring of adolescent quality improvement;
c. conducting evaluation and monitoring of elderly quality of life improvement;
d. conducting evaluation and monitoring of family economic improvement; and e. conducting evaluation and monitoring of family capability and skill improvement.

text:
Pasal 42

Penyediaan layanan bagi keluarga sebagaimana dimaksud dalam  Pasal 37 ayat (1) huruf meliputi:
a. komunikasi, informasi dan edukasi;
b. alat dan obat kontrasepsi;
c. pencatatan dan pelaporan pelayanan keluarga berencana; d. fasilitas sarana dan prasarana pelayanan kesehatan yang  memadai; dane. ruangan pojok ASI disetiap fasilitas umum.

translated_text:
Article 42

Provision of services for families as referred to in Article 37 paragraph (1) letter comprises:
a. communication, information and education;
b. contraceptive devices and medicines;
c. recording and reporting of family planning services; d. adequate health service facilities and infrastructure; and e. breastfeeding corner rooms in every public facility.

text:
Pasal 44

1. Selain Pemerintah Daerah, pihak swasta wajib menyediakan  ruangan pojok ASI;
2. Ruangan pojok ASI sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  merupakan ruangan yang layak dan memadai;
3. Pihak swasta yang tidak menyediakan ruangan pojok ASI  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dikenai sanksi administrasi  berupa:a. peringatan tertulis;
b. pembatasan kegiatan usaha;
c. pembekuan kegiatan usaha;
d. denda administrasi; dan/ataue. pencabutan izin.

translated_text:
Article 44

1. In addition to the Regional Government, private parties are obligated to provide breastfeeding corner rooms;
2. Breastfeeding corner rooms as referred to in paragraph (1) constitute proper and adequate rooms;
3. Private parties that do not provide breastfeeding corner rooms as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be subject to administrative sanctions in the form of: a. written warning;
b. limitation of business activities;
c. suspension of business activities;
d. administrative fine; and/or e. revocation of permit.

text:
Pasal 48

1. Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya pemenuhan hak anak  bertanggung jawab:a. memetapkan dan melaksanakan kebijakan serta program/  kegiatan pemenuhan hak anak;
b. menghormati dan menjamin hak asasi setiap anak dengan  tidak membedakan suku, agama, ras, golongan, jenis  kelamin, etnik, budaya dan bahasa, status hukum anak,  urutan kelahiran anak, dan kondisi fisik dan/atau mental;
c. menguatkan dan mengembangkan lembaga penyedia layanan  peningkatan kualitas keluarga dalam mewujudkan hak anak; d. menjamin perlindungan pemeliharaan dan kesejahteraan  anak dengan memperhatikan hak dan kewajiban orang tua,  wali atau orang lain yang secara hukum bertanggungjawab  terhadap anak;
e. menjamin hak anak untuk menyampaikan pendapat sesuai  dengan usia dan tingkat kecerdasan anak;
f. melakukan pengawasan dan pembinaan dalam rangka  penyelenggaraan pemenuhan hak anak; dang. melakukan kerjasama dengan pihak swasta dan/ atau LSM  dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan anak.
2. Tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya Perlindungan  anak sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh PD  yang menyelenggarakan Urusan Pemerintahan di bidang Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak.

translated_text:
Article 48

1. Regional Government in efforts to fulfill children's rights is responsible for: a. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for fulfillment of children's rights;
b. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every child without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnicity, culture and language, legal status of the child, birth order of the child, and physical and/or mental condition;
c. strengthening and developing service provider institutions for improving family quality in realizing children's rights; d. guaranteeing the protection, maintenance and welfare of children with due regard to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians or other persons legally responsible for the child;
e. guaranteeing the right of children to express opinions in accordance with the age and level of intelligence of the child;
f. conducting supervision and guidance in the context of implementing fulfillment of children's rights; and g. conducting cooperation with private parties and/or NGOs in implementing child protection.
2. The responsibility of the Regional Government in child protection efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by Regional Apparatus that administers Government Affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

text:
Pasal 55

1. Upaya promotif pelayanan kesehatan dasar sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 54 ayat (2) huruf a ditujukan untuk  meningkatkan derajat kesehatan secara lebih optimal.
2. Upaya promotif sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan  dengan memberikan sosialisasi atau penyuluhan kepada  masyarakat mengenai pola hidup sehat yang meliputi: a. pentingnya ASI ekslusif bagi bayi;
b. pentingnya imunisasi bagi balita;
c. pola hidup bersih;
d. pentingnya makanan bergizi; dane. bahaya narkoba dan merokok.
3. Selain upaya promotif sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2),  Pemerintah Daerah dapat melakukan kegiatan lain dalam rangka  penyelenggaraan kesehatan.

translated_text:
Article 55

1. Promotive efforts for basic health services as referred to in Article 54 paragraph (2) letter a are aimed at improving health status in a more optimal manner.
2. Promotive efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by providing socialization or counseling to the community regarding healthy lifestyle patterns which include: a. the importance of exclusive breastfeeding for infants;
b. the importance of immunization for toddlers;
c. clean living patterns;
d. the importance of nutritious food; ande. the dangers of drugs and smoking.
3. In addition to promotive efforts as referred to in paragraph (2), Regional Government may carry out other activities in the context of health provision.

text:
Pasal 56

1. Upaya preventif pelayanan kesehatan dasar sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 54 ayat (2) huruf a, ditujukan untuk  mencegah terjadinya penyakit atau permasalahannya kesehatan.
2. Upaya sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan dengan: a. mewajibkan pada ibu untuk pemberian ASI ekslusif pada bayi  sampai usia 6 (enam) bulan;
b. pemberian imunisasi dan vitamin gratis pada bayi dan balita; c. pemberian makanan bergizi kepada balita dari keluarga  kurang mampu;
d. mengoptimalkan peran posyandu untuk pelayanan  kiesehatan bagi ibu dan balita;
e. melakukan pemeriksaan kesehatan secara berkala; dan f. menyediakan sarana sanitasi dan air bersih disetiap sekolah.

translated_text:
Article 56

1. Preventive efforts for basic health services as referred to in Article 54 paragraph (2) letter a, are aimed at preventing the occurrence of disease or health problems.
2. Efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by: a. requiring mothers to provide exclusive breastfeeding to infants up to 6 (six) months of age;
b. provision of free immunization and vitamins to infants and toddlers; c. provision of nutritious food to toddlers from underprivileged families;
d. optimizing the role of posyandu for health services for mothers and toddlers;
e. conducting periodic health examinations; and f. providing sanitation facilities and clean water in every school.

text:
Pasal 59

1. Pemerintah Daerah wajib menyelenggarakan kesejahteraan sosial  bagi:a. anak yang berhadapan dengan hukum;
b. anak korban kekerasan yang tereksploitasi secara ekonomi  dan seksual, anak terlantar, anak korban penculikan dan  anak korban perdagangan orang;
c. anak yang tidak mempunyai orang tua dan diasuh oleh pihak  atau keluarga yang tidak mampu.  d. anak korban bencana alam atau bencana sosial; dan e. anak penyandang disabilitas.
2. Kesejahteraan sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat  berupa penyediaan layanan:a. kesehatan;
b. pendidikan;
c. bantuan hukum;
d. pendampingan;
e. bimbingan sosial, mental dan spiritual;
f. rehabilitasi sosial; dan/ ataug. reintegrasi.

translated_text:
Article 59

1. Regional Government is obliged to provide social welfare for:a. children in conflict with the law;
b. child victims of violence who are exploited economically and sexually, neglected children, child victims of kidnapping and child victims of trafficking in persons;
c. children who do not have parents and are cared for by parties or families who are unable.  d. child victims of natural disasters or social disasters; and e. children with disabilities.
2. Social welfare as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of provision of services:a. health;
b. education;
c. legal aid;
d. assistance;
e. social, mental and spiritual guidance;
f. social rehabilitation; and/org. reintegration.

text:
Pasal 61

Setiap orang/bahan yang mempekerjakan anak harus  memperlihatkan persyaratan:
a. berusia paling rendah 15 (lima belas) tahun;
b. mendapat persetujuan tertulis dari orang tua/ wali pekerja anak; c. memiliki perjanjian kerja tertulis antara majikan dengan orang tua/wali pekerja dan mendapat pengesahan dari instansi yang berwenang;
d. tidak mempekerjakan anak pada malam hari;
e. waktu kerja paling lama 3 (tiga) jam dalam sehari;
f. tidak dipekerjakan pada tempat atau lingkungan yang dapat  mengganggu proses tumbuh kembang anak, baik secara fisik,  mental, moral dan intelektual maupun kesehatan anak;
g. memberi kesempatan untuk mendapat pendidikan sesuai dengan  bakat dan minatnya;
h. mempekerjakan untuk jenis pekerjaan yang ringan; dan i. memberikan kesempatan libur satu hari dalam seminggu.

translated_text:
Article 61

Every person/entity that employs children must observe the requirements:
a. minimum age of 15 (fifteen) years;
b. obtain written consent from the parents/guardian of the child worker; c. have a written employment agreement between the employer and the parents/guardian of the worker and obtain validation from the authorized agency;
d. not employ children at night;
e. working time of maximum 3 (three) hours per day;
f. not be employed in a place or environment that can disrupt the child's growth and development process, whether physically, mentally, morally and intellectually or the child's health;
g. provide opportunities to obtain education in accordance with their talents and interests;
h. employ for light types of work; and i. provide one day off per week.

text:
Pasal 66

1. Dalam rangka pemenuhan hak anak secara terpadu dan  sistematis dan berkelanjutan Pemerintah Daerah menetapkan  Rencana Aksi Daerah Pembangunan Kabupaten Layak Anak.
2. Rencana Aksi Daerah Pembangunan Kabupaten Layak Anak  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), memuat tentang: a. konsep Kabupaten Layak Anak menyangkut dengan tujuan,  strategi dan peranan para pihak terkait;
b. hak anak;
c. pendekatan pengembangan Kabupaten Layak Anak.

translated_text:
Article 66

1. In the context of fulfilling children's rights in an integrated, systematic and sustainable manner, Regional Government establishes a Regional Action Plan for Child-Friendly Regency Development.
2. The Regional Action Plan for Child-Friendly Regency Development as referred to in paragraph (1), contains: a. the concept of Child-Friendly Regency concerning objectives, strategies and roles of related parties;
b. children's rights;
c. approach to developing a Child-Friendly Regency.

text:
Pasal 67

1. Rencana Aksi Daerah Pembangunan Kabupaten Layak anak  diarahkan pada pemenuhan hak anak yang terbagi dalam 5  (lima) kelompok sasaran, meliputi:a. hak sipil dan kebebasan;
b. lingkungan keluarga dan pengasuhan alternatif;
c. kesehatan dasar dan kesejahteraan;
d. pendidikan, pemanfaatan waktu luang, kegiatan budaya; dan e. perlindungan khusus.
2. Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai Rencana Aksi Daerah  Pembangunan Kabupaten Layak Anak sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1) diatur dalam Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 67

1. The Regional Action Plan for the Development of a Child-Friendly Regency is directed at the fulfillment of children's rights divided into 5 (five) target groups, comprising:a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, leisure time utilization, cultural activities; and e. special protection.
2. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan for the Development of a Child-Friendly Regency as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 68

1. Dalam rangka efektifitas pelaksanaan Rencana Aksi Daerah  Pembangunan Kabupaten Layak Anak di Daerah dibentuk Gugus  Tugas Kabupaten Layak Anak.
2. Pembentukan dan susunan keanggotaan Gugus Tugas Kabupaten layak anak ditetapkan dengan Keputusan Bupati.
3. Gugus Tugas Kabupaten layak Anak berkedudukan pada PD yang menyelenggarakan urusan pemerintahan di bidang  pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.
4. Gugus Tugas kabupaten layak Anak sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1), mempunyai tugas pokok:a. mengkoordinasikan pelaksanaan kebijakan dan  pengembangan kabupaten layak Anak;
b. melakukan sosialisasi, advokasi dan komunikasi informasi  dan edukasi kebijakan Kabupaten layak anak:c. mengumpulkan data dasar pengembangan Kabupaten layak  anak;
d. melakukan analisis kebutuhan yang bersumber dari data  dasar;
e. melakukan deseminasi data dasar;
f. menentukan fokus dan prioritas program dalam mewujudkan  Kabupaten Layak anak yang disesuaikan dengan potensi  daerah;
g. menyusun rencana aksi daerah kabupaten layak anak 5  (lima) tahunan dan mekanisme kerja; danh. melakukan monitoring, evaluasi dan pelaporan paling sedikit  1 (satu) tahun sekali.

translated_text:
Article 68

1. In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of the Regional Action Plan for the Development of a Child-Friendly Regency in the Region, a Child-Friendly Regency Task Force shall be established.
2. The establishment and membership composition of the Child-Friendly Regency Task Force shall be stipulated by Regent Decree.
3. The Child-Friendly Regency Task Force shall be domiciled at the Regional Agency that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
4. The Child-Friendly Regency Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) shall have the following principal duties:a. coordinating the implementation of policies and development of a Child-Friendly Regency;
b. conducting socialization, advocacy and communication, information and education on Child-Friendly Regency policies:c. collecting baseline data for the development of a Child-Friendly Regency;
d. conducting needs analysis sourced from baseline data;
e. disseminating baseline data;
f. determining the focus and priority of programs in realizing a Child-Friendly Regency adjusted to regional potential;
g. preparing a 5 (five) year regional action plan for a Child-Friendly Regency and work mechanisms; andh. conducting monitoring, evaluation and reporting at least once (1) a year.

text:
BAB VIII

SISTEM DATA GENDER DAN ANAK

Pasal 70

Pemerintah daerah dalam rangka memberikan perlindungan terhadap  anak:
a. melakukan pencegahan kekerasan terhadap anak dengan  mengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat;
b. melakukan sosialisasi seminar dan penyuluhan mengenai  perlindungan dan hak anak;
c. mengembangkan model sekolah ramah anak;
d. menyediakan fasilitas umum yang ramah dan aman untuk anak; e. menyusun database dan informasi tentang tindak kekerasan  terhadap anak;
f. melakukan pemetaan lokasi dan wilayah yang rawan terjadinya  kekerasan terhadap anak;
g. melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama dalam pencegahan  terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak anak;
h. penguatan fungsi lembaga atau organisasi yang bergerak di bidang  perlindungan anak; dani. mendorong kepedulian masyarakat akan pentingnya perlindungan  terhadap anak dengan membentuk pendampingan perlindungan  perempuan dan anak.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VIII

GENDER AND CHILD DATA SYSTEM

Article 70

The regional government in order to provide protection to children:
a. prevents violence against children by optimizing the role of customary institutions;
b. conducts socialization, seminars and counseling regarding child protection and rights;
c. develops child-friendly school models;
d. provides public facilities that are friendly and safe for children; e. compiles databases and information on acts of violence against children;
f. conducts mapping of locations and areas prone to violence against children;
g. conducts coordination and cooperation in preventing violations of children's rights;
h. strengthens the function of institutions or organizations working in the field of child protection; andi. encourages public awareness of the importance of child protection by establishing assistance for the protection of women and children.

text:
Pasal 72

1. Peran serta masyarakat dalam upaya perlindungan terhadap  perempuan dan anak antara lain:a. berpartisipasi dalam pencegahan dan memberikan dukungan  terhadap pengembangan program pencegahan terjadinya  pelanggaran terhadap hak perempuan dan anak;
b. memberikan perlindungan kepada korban dan pertolongan  darurat;
c. memberikan informasi dan/atau melaporkan terjadinya  pelanggaran hak perempuan dan anak kepada pihak yang  berwenang;
d. mengawasi proses penegakan hukum terhadap kasus pelanggaran hak perempuan dan anak; dane. pembentukan Kelompok Perlindungan Anak Terpadu Berbasis  Masyarakat (PATBM).
2. Keluarga dan orang tua berperan untuk melindungi serta  mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak perempuan dan  anak.
3. Peran serta pihak perusahaan swasta dalam upaya perlindungan  terhadap perempuan dan anak antara lain:a. sosialisasi dan advokasi terkait perlindungan anak di  lingkungan perusahaannya;
b. mengakomodir program-program pencegahan kekerasan  terhadap anak melalui dana CSR;
c. mengakomodir program-program perlindungan anak korban  kekerasan melalui dana CSR;
d. memfasilitasi tempat/rumah aman bagi anak korban  kekerasan di lingkungan perusahaan; dane. menyediakan layanan pengaduan bagi anak korban  kekerasan.
4. Peran serta masyarakat, keluarga dan orang tua sebagaimana  dimaksud pada ayat (1) dan ayat (2) berdasarkan peraturan  perundang-undangan dan nilai-nilai kearifan lokal masyarakat  setempat.

translated_text:
Article 72

1. Community participation in efforts to protect women and children includes, among others:a. participating in prevention and providing support for the development of programs to prevent violations of the rights of women and children;
b. providing protection to victims and emergency assistance;
c. providing information and/or reporting violations of the rights of women and children to the competent authorities;
d. supervising the law enforcement process for cases of violations of the rights of women and children; ande. establishing Community-Based Integrated Child Protection Groups (PATBM).
2. Families and parents play a role in protecting and preventing violations of the rights of women and children.
3. The participation of private companies in efforts to protect women and children includes, among others:a. socialization and advocacy related to child protection in their company environment;
b. accommodating programs for the prevention of violence against children through CSR funds;
c. accommodating programs for the protection of child victims of violence through CSR funds;
d. facilitating safe places/houses for child victims of violence in the company environment; ande. providing complaint services for child victims of violence.
4. The participation of the community, families and parents as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be based on laws and regulations and the values of local wisdom of the local community.

text:
Pasal 73

1. Dalam rangka pencegahan terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak  perempuan, masyarakat:a. mengawasi berbagai kondisi yang terjadi di lingkungannya  yang dapat menimbulkan pelanggaran terhadap hak  perempuan;
b. meningkatkan kepedulian terhadap hak perempuan; c. menguatkan peran, organisasi kemasyarakatan, keagamaan  dan lingkungan keluarga; dand. mencegah pernikahan di bawah tangan.
2. Dalam rangka pencegahan terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak  anak, masyarakat:a. mengawasi berbagai kondisi yang terjadi dilingkungannya  yang dapat menimbulkan pelanggaran terhadap hak  perempuan;
b. meningkatkan kepedulian terhadap pelanggaran hak anak; c. menguatkan peran organisasi kemasyarakatan, keagamaan  dan lingkungan keluarga; dand. mencegah terjadinya perkawinan pada usia dini.

translated_text:
Article 73

1. In order to prevent violations of women's rights, the community:a. monitors various conditions occurring in their environment that may give rise to violations of women's rights;
b. increases awareness of women's rights; c. strengthens the role of community, religious and family environment organizations; andd. prevents unregistered marriages.
2. In order to prevent violations of children's rights, the community:a. monitors various conditions occurring in their environment that may give rise to violations of women's rights;
b. increases awareness of violations of children's rights; c. strengthens the role of community, religious and family environment organizations; andd. prevents early marriage.

text:
Pasal 75

1. Orang tua dalam upaya perlindungan terhadap hak anak  berperan:a. mengasuh, memelihara, mendidik dan melindungi anak; b. menumbuhkembangkan anak sesuai dengan kemampuan,  bakat dan minatnya;
c. memberikan pendidikan formal dan non formal;
d. membimbing anak berperilaku sesuai dengan agama. Etika dan moral serta adat istiadat; dane. mencegah terjadinya perkawinan pada usia dini.
2. Dalam hal orang tua tidak ada, atau tidak diketahui  keberadaannya, atau karena suatu sebab, tidak dapat  melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggung jawabnya, maka  kewajiban dan tanggungjawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat  (1) dapat beralih pada keluarga.

translated_text:
Article 75

1. Parents in efforts to protect children's rights play a role in:a. caring for, maintaining, educating and protecting children; b. developing children according to their abilities, talents and interests;
c. providing formal and non-formal education;
d. guiding children to behave in accordance with religion, ethics and morals as well as customs; ande. preventing early marriage.
2. In the event that parents are absent, or their whereabouts are unknown, or due to any reason, cannot carry out their obligations and responsibilities, then the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) may be transferred to the family.

text:
BAB X

PEMBINAAN DAN PENGAWASAN

Pasal 76

1. Pembinaan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak dilakukan oleh Pemerintah Daerah.
2. Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat dilakukan  dalam bentuk:a. memberikan pelatihan bagi aparat pemerintah dan penegak  hukum tentang pencegahan;
b. memberikan pelatihan bagi tokoh agama, tokoh masyarakat,  tokoh adat, tenaga pendidik, jurnalis dan pengelola media  dalam rangka mencegah kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan  anak;
c. memberikan pelatihan kepada tenaga kesehatan yang  memberikan pelayanan kesehatan kepada perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan di puskesmas, unit pelayanan  terpadu dan rumah sakit umum;
d. memberikan pelatihan kepada petugas rehabilitasi sosial dan  petugas bimbingan rohani dalam rangka melindungi  perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan; dane. melakukan peningkatan profesional petugas, pengelola data  kasus kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak di  puskesmas, unit pelayanan terpadu dan rumah sakit.
3. Bupati berwenang melakukan pembinaan dalam penyelengaraan  pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.

translated_text:
CHAPTER X

GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 76

1. Guidance on women's empowerment and child protection shall be conducted by the Regional Government.
2. Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) may be conducted in the form of:a. providing training for government officials and law enforcers on prevention;
b. providing training for religious leaders, community leaders, customary leaders, educators, journalists and media managers in order to prevent violence against women and children;
c. providing training to health workers who provide health services to women and child victims of violence at community health centers, integrated service units and general hospitals;
d. providing training to social rehabilitation officers and spiritual guidance officers in order to protect women and child victims of violence; ande. improving the professionalism of officers, managers of case data on violence against women and children at community health centers, integrated service units and hospitals.
3. The Regent is authorized to conduct guidance in the implementation of women's empowerment and child protection.
